  "notes": "{暁|あかつき} has both literal (dawn) and figurative (occasion) meanings.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {暁|あかつき}の{空|そら}: dawn sky\n- 〜の{暁|あかつき}には: when ~, on the occasion of ~\n- {成功|せいこう}の{暁|あかつき}には: when success is achieved\n\nUSAGE:\nSense 2 is often used in formal or literary contexts to express anticipation of a future event.\n\nREGISTER:\nBoth senses are somewhat formal or literary.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {曙|あけぼの}: dawn (more poetic)\n- {夜明|よあ}け: daybreak (more common)\n- {明|あ}け{方|がた}: early morning",
